---
description: Data layer — data sources, repository implementations, failure mapping
globs: packages/*/lib/data/**/*.dart
alwaysApply: false
---

The data layer implements the domain repository interfaces. It owns data sources, API clients, JSON parsing, and caching. Map errors to `Failure` and return `Left`; return `Right` on success — do not throw for expected errors.

- Put remote/cache I/O behind a **data source** collaborator in `data/sources/`; a repository composes data sources rather than performing I/O itself.
- Data sources are repository collaborators, **not** domain strategies — never place them in `domain/strategies/`.
- Keep DTOs and JSON parsing in `data/`; the domain layer must never see transport types.

```dart
// data/sources/item_data_source.dart
abstract interface class ItemDataSource {
  Future<Either<Failure, List<Item>>> fetchItems();
}

// data/sources/remote_item_data_source.dart
final class RemoteItemDataSource implements ItemDataSource {
  const RemoteItemDataSource(this._api);
  final CatalogApiClient _api;

  @override
  Future<Either<Failure, List<Item>>> fetchItems() async { /* ... */ }
}

// data/repositories/item_repository_impl.dart
class ItemRepositoryImpl implements ItemRepository {
  const ItemRepositoryImpl(this._dataSource);
  final ItemDataSource _dataSource;

  @override
  Future<Either<Failure, List<Item>>> getItemList() =>
      _dataSource.fetchItems();
}
```
